              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does the Wahoo treadmill have a screen?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. It has a device shelf for a laptop up to 17 inches, bottle holders and USB-C charging, and is designed to be used with an app on your own device.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What does the KICKR RUN need to be installed?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Wahoo requires a dedicated 120 V, 60 Hz circuit with a 15 or 20 amp non-GFCI breaker and matching outlet, 80 inches of clear space behind it and 24 inches each side, and in-home setup, which is included. It weighs 429 lb by Wahoo’s figure and does not fold.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What warranty comes with the Wahoo KICKR RUN?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Wahoo’s product page lists a one-year warranty. One independent review describes five years on the frame and one year on parts and labour, so confirm the terms for your purchase in writing.
              </p>
