        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Wahoo KICKR RUN</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The KICKR RUN is expensive, heavy and close to non-returnable. These are the ways buyers get it wrong.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not checking the circuit before ordering</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Wahoo requires a dedicated 120 V circuit with a 15 or 20 amp non-GFCI breaker. Many garages and basements do not have one where the treadmill will go, and an extension cord is not an answer. Have an electrician look before delivery day, not after.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the 250 lb rating</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A 250 lb maximum user weight is low for any running treadmill, let alone a $7,000 one. Runners near it, or households where a heavier person will also use it, should choose a machine rated to 350 or 400 lb.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting it to follow Peloton or iFIT classes</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Peloton and Strava receive the KICKR RUN’s data but do not change its speed or grade, and iFIT is not supported. If you already pay for a class platform, its own treadmill will follow the classes; the KICKR RUN is built for Zwift, Kinomap, Wahoo’s app and structured pace plans.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying at full price in a hurry</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The KICKR RUN launched at $4,999 and has been discounted heavily at times since, including reported sale prices around $5,250 in late 2025. With a $750 restocking fee on returns, it pays to buy once, at a good price, after measuring everything.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

